    "reason": "The upgrade guide [ev-2df1b23f32ac] says HTTP/3 can now be enabled on entry points without `experimental.http3`. That option is removed, and leaving it set would prevent Traefik from starting. So an environment is exposed only if it still sets the experimental http3 option in its static configuration (CLI flag or values key). The proposed runtime-behavior-gap undecidable leaf is wrong: using HTTP/3 on entry points does not cause exposure, and the condition can be read from configuration. Inside an \"any\", that leaf would wrongly flag every environment as possibly exposed [ev-177a6106bc02].",
